# The Raspberry Pi 5 image.
#
# This is not the ISO's package list with a different arch on it. The ISO
# ships a live installer; this ships the installed system, because an ARM
# board has no installer to run - the image IS the result.
#
# Four things the x86_64 image has cannot exist here, and their absence is
# the reason this file is separate rather than generated:
#
#   - no linux-cachyos: CachyOS publishes no ARM repositories, so there is
#     no v3 userland and no CachyOS kernel. This is plain Arch Linux ARM.
#   - no systemd-boot: a Pi boots its own firmware off the FAT partition.
#   - no TPM and no LUKS: there is no installer to enrol a keyslot, so
#     tpm2-tools would ship a tool for hardware the image never uses.
#   - no chwd: it comes from the cachyos repo and is x86_64 only.

# base
base
# linux-rpi and the board firmware are NOT listed here: the rootfs ships
# linux-aarch64, and the two conflict on `linux`, so build-image.sh
# replaces one with the other before this list is installed. Listing them
# again would just be the conflict in a second place.
linux-firmware
sudo
which
less

# our own
ashlaros-settings
ashlaros-branding
ashlaros-browser-settings
ashlaros-keyring
ashlaros-mirrorlist
# ashlaros-release carries os-release and the hook that keeps it; the
# snapshot wrapper is a binary inside ashlaros-settings, not a package
ashlaros-release

# desktop
#
# sway, waybar, foot, rofi, mako, grim and the rest are not listed: they
# are depends= of ashlaros-settings above, and listing them again would
# be a second place to keep in step. Only what the settings package does
# NOT pull belongs here.
#
# rofi in particular is plain `rofi`, not `rofi-wayland` - that package
# was folded upstream and exists in no repository today; rofi provides it
# since 2.0, which is what the settings PKGBUILD already says.
greetd
greetd-tuigreet
firefox

# session plumbing
networkmanager
bluez
bluez-utils
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
xorg-xwayland
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland
gnome-keyring
polkit-gnome
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-user-dirs

# files, printing, discovery - the same set the installer picks, because
# what a user sees is meant to be the same desktop
pcmanfm-qt
gvfs
gvfs-mtp
gvfs-smb
gvfs-nfs
cups
cups-pk-helper
system-config-printer
libusb
nss-mdns

# cli
ripgrep
fd
bat
eza
tldr
plocate
vim
nano
git

# system
# mise-bin rather than mise: Arch's mise is x86_64 only and Arch Linux ARM
# has neither, so this is the vendored one - which is the whole point of
# carrying it (#10). DESKTOP_PACKAGES cannot serve here; that list is
# x86_64 by construction.
mise-bin
ufw
power-profiles-daemon
kernel-modules-hook
# growing the root partition on first boot needs both
parted
e2fsprogs
# the image is written to a card; a user who wants to check it wants this
rsync
openssh
